{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And these.</b> After he mentioned the generations of Ishmael, he returned to mention the generations of Isaac, who are Esau and Jacob. Some say that the reason for \"begot Isaac\" is that he resembled his father, and all who saw him would testify that Abraham begot him. Some say that the reason for \"begot\" is \"raised and brought up,\" as in \"were born upon Joseph's knees\" (Genesis 50:23), and the proof is that he said, \"and sent them away from Isaac his son\" (Genesis 25:6)."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:45:45.484107355Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}